        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. New Braunfels is our home base, and we serve the surrounding Hill Country corridor including Canyon Lake, Gruene, Fischer, Wimberley, San Marcos, Seguin, and the entire Comal and Guadalupe County area. We've completed full home theater and outdoor AV installs at lakefront properties on Canyon Lake and estate homes throughout the Hill Country. Distance is not a factor. We come to you."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you install outdoor speakers and a TV by the pool?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes, and it's one of the most common requests we get from New Braunfels homeowners. Outdoor entertainment setups typically include weather-rated in-ground or surface-mounted speakers for pool and patio coverage, a weatherproof TV on the covered patio or outdoor kitchen, and optional app control so you can manage everything from your phone. We run all wiring cleanly through the structure, no exposed conduit running across your patio. Texas summers are built for outdoor entertaining, and a properly installed outdoor AV system runs for years without issues."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Can you pre-wire a new home during construction?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. Pre-wire during rough-in is the right time to do it, running cable through open walls costs a fraction of what it costs post-drywall. We work directly with custom home builders and general contractors in New Braunfels and the Hill Country to install structured wiring, speaker wire, HDMI runs, and networking cable before the walls close. If you're building a home in Vintage Oaks, Solms Ranch, or anywhere in Comal County, call us before framing is complete."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What's the difference between a media room and a dedicated home theater?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "A media room is a multipurpose space, usually a living room or bonus room with a large TV or projector and a good sound system. Light control is partial, the room serves other purposes, and the seating isn't tiered. A dedicated home theater is a purpose-built room: blacked-out walls, acoustic treatment, raked or tiered seating, a projection screen, and a full surround sound system calibrated for that specific room. Both are great, the right choice depends on how you use the space and your budget. We build both."
      }
    },
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "Do you service or repair AV systems you didn't install?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "Yes. We work on systems we didn't install all the time: home control systems from installers who are no longer around, Crestron systems that need reprogramming, home theaters where the previous owner left undocumented equipment, and general AV setups that stopped working. If it can be diagnosed and fixed, we'll tell you honestly. If it's beyond repair, we'll tell you that too and give you options. We serve the New Braunfels and Hill Country area for AV repair and system rescue."
      }
    },
  ],
};

